## Steps

1. Manifest check: `cd ~/Desktop/handoff/storytime-l2u2-w15-candidates-r2 && sha256sum -c MANIFEST.txt`
   gives 5 OK and 0 FAILED. `MANIFEST.txt` SHA-256 is
   `225e440e5b7d8cf00307f8d81d92313b6d4befd7cc4f4508fa680384e2ca4d73`.
2. Script `RUNS/t61-w15-r2-coverage.py` follows the style of
   `jr-green-t113-check-songs-r2.py`: `norm_words`, `probe`, `pcm`, and a faster-whisper
   `small` transcript with int8, cpu, local files only, language en, word times on,
   `condition_on_previous_text` off, VAD off, beam 5, temperature 0.0, and no prompt.
   The loop rule is one word 10 times or more in a row. A LOOP take also gets the `base` model.
   The script writes `songs-transcripts/w15-r2-c1.json`, `-c2.json`, and `-c3.json`.
3. First run, one heavy job (`HEAVY_MIN_AVAIL_MB=1500 HEAVY_PREFLIGHT_WAIT_S=5400`) with the
   venv python. The transcript files came out with 72, 64, and 72 words, and durations
   67.474, 65.829, and 67.370 s at 44100 Hz. No take was a LOOP.
   The first scoring used a time cursor ("words after the end of the previous matched line").
   That cursor held the fault:
   - c3 held all 13 lines in order and scored 0 of 13. Line 2 "Look," starts at 13.08 s, the
     same time as the end of line 1 "beep" at 13.08 s, so the time cursor dropped the token
     and every later line failed.
   - c2 held the ending "Wave goodbye, time to go home" from 58.0 s and scored line 13 at
     0.00, because the missed lines 11 and 12 blocked the time cursor.
4. Fix per the orchestrator (scoring only; the transcribe settings did not change):
   - a token index cursor in place of the time cursor;
   - start offsets 0 to 8 tokens for each line, with lookahead 3 tokens;
   - a line at 0.8 or more is accepted and moves the cursor; a missed line keeps the cursor;
   - `--score-only` re-scores the 3 saved transcripts and loads no speech model;
   - `faster_whisper` imports inside `load_model` only.
5. Second run, a light run on saved JSON:
   `python3 -I RUNS/t61-w15-r2-coverage.py --score-only --capture RUNS/t61-w15-r2-coverage.txt`.
   Exit 0. The capture file is 50 lines, SHA-256
   `a5d8a57784452ef418928065faaaaf5d4f23da716b25e3dbeb93515bf8d55990`.
   No heavy-run and no new transcription.
6. Transcript proof: the 3 transcript files hold equal SHA-256 before and after the run.
   - c1 `9ba7b3ea004f58a8a7fb8ae17efea61f71f67bbd9753fd4a4bbaf544ec70294b`
   - c2 `6b862180a520b04629b5255879df31648acb2662c5f8964c30783573976887cf`
   - c3 `16fcaa2ae2a1e0287b43df258929bfcd2e5d05c7776adeedfd3641b2b1f622f8`

